// The sculpt package's booleans, checked with the testing package against
// values worked out by hand; only a failure prints, so booleans.out holds the
// summary alone. Every result is checked valid, closed (no edge with a face
// on one side only) and of the volume worked out, by the divergence theorem.
//
// A is the cube cage of size 1, [-1, 1]^3: vertex x + 2y + 4z (each 0 for -1,
// 1 for +1), faces back (z-) 0, front (z+) 1, left (x-) 2, right (x+) 3,
// bottom (y-) 4, top (y+) 5. Each quad is cut into two triangles from its
// first corner (the front face along y = x).
//
// - Exact predicates: (0.5 + 2^-53, 0.5), (12, 12), (24, 24), Kettner et
//   al.'s classroom example, whose orientation is (11.5 - u) 23.5 - 11.5
//   (23.5 - u) = -12u for u = 2^-53, below what an f64 evaluation can resolve:
//   -1, and its mirror image across the diagonal +1. A point an ulp to either
//   side of y = x at 0.5 is -1 or +1, one on it 0. Far out (2^40), a point
//   2^-20 off the line rounds onto it (0) and one an ulp (2^-12) off is +1. A
//   point 2^-60 in front of a triangle is +1, behind its turned-over twin -1,
//   in its plane 0; swapping two corners flips a sign.
// - Overlapping cubes, B = A moved by (0.5, 0.25, 0.375): B is [-0.5, 1.5] x
//   [-0.75, 1.25] x [-0.625, 1.375]. The intersection is the box [-0.5, 1] x
//   [-0.75, 1] x [-0.625, 1], 1.5 x 1.75 x 1.625 = 4.265625: 8 vertices, 12
//   edges, 6 faces, three of them A's (front, right, top, at A's corner
//   (1, 1, 1), which is inside B) and three B's (back, left, bottom, at B's
//   corner (-0.5, -0.75, -0.625), inside A). The union, 16 - 4.265625 =
//   11.734375: A's 7 corners outside B, B's 7 outside A, and the 6 points
//   where the edges from those two inner corners cross the other's faces, 20
//   vertices; A's 6 faces (3 notched into L-shaped hexagons) and B's 6, 12;
//   so 30 edges. The difference, 8 - 4.265625 = 3.734375: A's 7 corners, B's
//   inner corner, the 6 crossings, 14 vertices; A's 6 faces and B's 3 faces
//   at its inner corner, 9; 21 edges. The intersection's corner (1, -0.75,
//   -0.625) is a new vertex, exact in f32.
// - Touching cubes, B = A moved by (2, 0, 0), meeting in the face x = 1:
//   the union is the box [-1, 3] x [-1, 1]^2, volume 16, its sides each A's
//   face and B's face meeting along x = 1: 12 vertices, 20 edges, 10 faces;
//   nothing of the two touching faces is left. The intersection is empty and
//   says nothing. The difference is A exactly: 8 vertices, 6 faces, A's
//   positions.
// - Identical meshes: A u A and A n A are A (8, 12, 6, every position and
//   face A's, bit for bit); A - A is empty. Likewise a lathed torus, 24 x 32
//   quads, whose inner vertices are saddles: its union with itself is itself.
// - Disjoint, B = A moved by (3, 0.5, 0): the union is A's faces then B's,
//   each as it was (16, 24, 12); the difference is A; the intersection empty.
// - Coplanar faces: a box [-0.5, 0.5]^2 x [0, 1] flush with A's front face.
//   The difference is a pocket, volume 7: A's 8 corners, the pocket's rim 4 and
//   floor 4, 16 vertices; A's 5 whole faces, the front face round the pocket
//   as 2 faces (a square with a hole is at least 2 polygons), 4 walls and the
//   floor, 12 faces; 26 edges (16 - 26 + 12 = 2). The union is A, the box's
//   front cap set into A's front face as a face of its own (it keeps the box's
//   face values): 12 vertices, 18 edges, 8 faces, volume 8. The intersection
//   is the box, volume 1, 8, 12, 6. Flush at both ends (z from -1 to 1), the
//   difference is a square hole through A, volume 6: 16 vertices, 12 faces,
//   genus 1, so 28 edges.
// - Partly coplanar, B the box [0, 2] x [-1, 1]^2: union the box [-1, 2] x
//   [-1, 1]^2, volume 12, each long side A's face and B's meeting along x =
//   0: 12 vertices, 20 edges, 10 faces; difference and intersection each a box
//   of volume 4, 8, 12, 6.
// - A prism through A: a 16-gon of radius 0.5 centred at (0.1, 0.05) extruded
//   along z from -2 to 2. Its section's area S is (16 / 2) 0.5^2 sin(2 pi /
//   16) = 0.76536686 (worked from the f32 corners, it agrees to 10^-6).
//   Difference 8 - 2S = 6.4692663: A's 8 corners, the two rings of 16 where
//   the prism's edges cross the front and back faces, and on each of those
//   faces the 2 points where its diagonal crosses the prism's walls, 44; A's
//   4 sides, the front and back faces each as 2 pieces round the hole (the
//   diagonal crosses it twice), the 16 walls inside, 24; genus 1, so 68
//   edges. Union 8 + 2S: 8 + 32 ring + 32 end + 4 = 76 vertices; 4 sides + 4
//   pieces + 32 wall pieces (each wall's two stubs) + 2 caps = 42 faces; 116
//   edges. Intersection 2S: the 32 ring vertices, 16 walls and the two discs,
//   each one face (the diagonal's two pieces of a disc join again, and the
//   points where it met the ring, now on just two edges in a line, go): 32,
//   48, 18.
// - A pocket wholly inside one triangle of the front face, the box [0.3,
//   0.6] x [-0.6, -0.3] x [0.5, 1.5] taken away (its outline crosses no
//   edge, so the face's piece has a hole and is cut into triangles, then
//   joined again): volume 8 - 0.045 = 7.955, 16 vertices, 12 faces (the
//   front face as 2), 26 edges; the front face's pieces' areas add to 4 -
//   0.09 = 3.91. Union 8.045, intersection 0.045.
// - Touching along an edge, B the box [1, 3]^2 x [-1, 1]: the union, volume
//   16, is two cubes sharing an edge, which no manifold can be; it is kept
//   manifold by edges of no length, and one line says so. The difference is
//   A; the intersection is empty.
// - Two lathed tori (24 x 32), the second turned and moved: vol(A u B) +
//   vol(A n B) = 2 vol(A) and vol(A - B) + vol(A n B) = vol(A), to 10^-5
//   relative; every result valid and closed, nothing reported.
// - The same result whatever the order: B's faces listed backward and its
//   vertices renumbered (each face keeping its corners from the same first
//   corner) give the same faces, each as the cycle of its corners' positions,
//   as a set.
// - The same bits twice: a union run twice gives every list equal.
// - Channels: A has vertex "w" = x + 2y + 3z, face "id" 0 to 5, corner "uv"
//   (x, y) of the corner's position, edge "crease" 2 on its edge from vertex 3
//   to 7 (x = 1, y = 1, along z), vertex "weight" fill 1 at 0.5; B, the
//   overlapping cube, has "w" likewise, face "id" 10 to 15, corner "uv" alike,
//   no crease and no weight. In the intersection every vertex's w is x + 2y +
//   3z of its position (blended linearly along an edge, so exact to 10^-5),
//   every corner's uv is its position's (x, y) (blended barycentrically in its
//   triangle), the ids are A's 1, 3, 5 and B's 10, 12, 14; the crease edge's
//   piece from (1, 1, 1) to (1, 1, -0.625) keeps 2 and every other edge has 0;
//   B's vertex (-0.5, -0.75, -0.625) has weight 1 (the fill), A's (1, 1, 1)
//   0.5. With 'crease' 3, the 6 edges on the curve have crease 3 and the
//   crease edge still 2; on two meshes with no crease channel, one is made,
//   3 on the 6 curve edges and 0 elsewhere. A type clash (A's vertex "w"
//   against B's face Vec2 "w") is refused with join's line and the result
//   still made.
// - Refused: an open quad ("is not closed", nothing made); a cube with every
//   face turned over ("faces inward").
// - Slivers cleaned: a box [-0.25, 0.5] x [-0.75, 0.75] x [0.5, 0.75] on a box
//   [0.25, 0.75] x [-0.75, 0.25] x [0, 0.5], face to face over [0.25, 0.5] x
//   [-0.75, 0.25] and sharing the plane y = -0.75, where the perturbation's
//   walls of no height once left a spike in the lower box's top: the union,
//   0.28125 + 0.25 = 0.53125, is the upper box's 8 corners, the lower's 8, and
//   the point (0.5, 0.25, 0.5) where the upper box's bottom edge crosses the
//   lower box's top edge, 17 vertices; each box's 6 faces (the upper's bottom
//   an L of 6 corners, the lower's top a quad), 12; so 27 edges; no face has
//   two corners at one point or two sides overlapping on a line. A plus sign
//   of two bars [-1, 1] x [-0.25, 0.25] x [0, 0.5] and [-0.25, 0.25] x [-1, 1]
//   x [0, 0.5], sharing their top and bottom planes, 0.5 + 0.5 - 0.125 =
//   0.875, slotted through its top by [-0.1, 0.1] x [-2, 2] x [0.25, 1], less
//   0.2 x 2 x 0.25 = 0.1: 0.775, clean, and used again (its intersection with
//   a box holding it is itself). Every result above that should be clean is
//   checked so.
// - Two boxes touching along an edge, kept manifold by edges of no length,
//   cannot be an input: such an edge's triangle has no area, and the refusal
//   says so.

mod booleans;

import testing use *;
import collections use *;
import geomath use *;
import mesh use *;
import sculpt use *;

let near = 0.00001;

fn counts(m: &PolyMesh, nv: i64, ne: i64, nf: i64, label: &Array[u8]) {
  expectInt(i64.from(m.vertexCount()), nv, label);
  expectInt(i64.from(m.edgeCount()), ne, label);
  expectInt(i64.from(m.faceCount()), nf, label);
}

// Valid, closed, and of the volume given
fn solid(m: &PolyMesh, vol: f64, label: &Array[u8]) {
  let problems = m.validate();
  expectInt(i64.from(problems.len()), 0, label);
  var open = 0i64;
  var h = 0usize;
  while h < m.hFace.len() {
    if *m.hFace[h] == NoIndex { open = open + 1; }
    h = h + 1usize;
  }
  expectInt(open, 0, label);
  expectFloat(volume(m), vol, 0.00001, label);
}

// Valid, closed, of the volume given, and no face of no area
fn clean(m: &PolyMesh, vol: f64, label: &Array[u8]) {
  solid(m, vol, label);
  expectInt(degenerateFaces(m), 0, label);
}

// The signed volume, by the divergence theorem over each face's fan, in f64
fn volume(m: &PolyMesh) f64 {
  var sum = 0.0;
  var f = 0usize;
  while f < m.faceCount() {
    let pts = m.facePositions(u32.from(f));
    var i = 1usize;
    while i + 1usize < pts.len() {
      let a = DVec3.from(*pts[0usize]);
      let b = DVec3.from(*pts[i]);
      let c = DVec3.from(*pts[i + 1usize]);
      sum = sum + a.x * (b.y * c.z - b.z * c.y) + a.y * (b.z * c.x - b.x * c.z) + a.z * (b.x * c.y - b.y * c.x);
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    f = f + 1usize;
  }
  sum / 6.0
}

// A face's area, by Newell's normal
fn faceArea(m: &PolyMesh, f: u32) f64 {
  let pts = m.facePositions(f);
  var nx = 0.0;
  var ny = 0.0;
  var nz = 0.0;
  var i = 0usize;
  while i < pts.len() {
    let p = DVec3.from(*pts[i]);
    let q = DVec3.from(*pts[(i + 1usize) % pts.len()]);
    nx = nx + (p.y - q.y) * (p.z + q.z);
    ny = ny + (p.z - q.z) * (p.x + q.x);
    nz = nz + (p.x - q.x) * (p.y + q.y);
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  0.5 * (nx * nx + ny * ny + nz * nz).sqrt()
}

fn placed(m: PolyMesh, t: Transform3) PolyMesh {
  var parts = List[PolyMesh].empty();
  parts.push(m);
  var places = List[Transform3].empty();
  places.push(t);
  var problems = List[String].empty();
  joinPlaced(&parts, &places, &mut problems)
}

fn moved(m: PolyMesh, d: Vec3) PolyMesh {placed(m, new Transform3(d, Quat.identity(), new Vec3(1., 1., 1.)))}

fn box(lo: Vec3, hi: Vec3) PolyMesh {
  placed(PolyMesh.cube(0.5), new Transform3((lo + hi) * 0.5, Quat.identity(), hi - lo))
}

fn torus(major: f32, minor: f32, around: u32, steps: u32) PolyMesh {
  var pts = List[Vec2].empty();
  var i = 0u32;
  while i < around {
    let a = 2. * pi * f32.from(i) / f32.from(around);
    pts.push(new Vec2(major + minor * cos(a), minor * sin(a)));
    i = i + 1u32;
  }
  let prof = Profile.fromPoints(pts.view(), true);
  lathe(&prof, new Vec3(0., 1., 0.), 2. * pi, steps)
}

fn prism(sides: u32, radius: f32, x: f32, y: f32, z0: f32, z1: f32) PolyMesh {
  let prof = Profile.circle(sides, radius);
  let m = extrude(&prof, new Vec3(0., 0., z1 - z0), 1u32, true);
  moved(m, new Vec3(x, y, z0))
}

fn hasPoint(m: &PolyMesh, x: f32, y: f32, z: f32) bool {
  var v = 0usize;
  while v < m.positions.len() {
    let p = *m.positions[v];
    if p.x == x && p.y == y && p.z == z { return true; }
    v = v + 1usize;
  }
  false
}

// Every position and every face's corners the same, exactly
fn sameShape(a: &PolyMesh, b: &PolyMesh, label: &Array[u8]) {
  expectInt(i64.from(a.vertexCount()), i64.from(b.vertexCount()), label);
  expectInt(i64.from(a.faceCount()), i64.from(b.faceCount()), label);
  if a.vertexCount() != b.vertexCount() || a.faceCount() != b.faceCount() { return; }
  var same = true;
  var v = 0usize;
  while v < a.positions.len() {
    let p = *a.positions[v];
    let q = *b.positions[v];
    if p.x != q.x || p.y != q.y || p.z != q.z { same = false; }
    v = v + 1usize;
  }
  var f = 0usize;
  while f < a.faceCount() {
    let va = a.faceVertices(u32.from(f));
    let vb = b.faceVertices(u32.from(f));
    if va.len() != vb.len() { same = false; } else {
      var i = 0usize;
      while i < va.len() {
        if *va[i] != *vb[i] { same = false; }
        i = i + 1usize;
      }
    }
    f = f + 1usize;
  }
  expect(same, label);
}

// The faces, each as the cycle of its corners' positions started at its
// lexicographically least, as strings sorted, joined: a set of faces
fn faceSet(m: &PolyMesh) List[String] {
  var out = List[String].empty();
  var f = 0usize;
  while f < m.faceCount() {
    let pts = m.facePositions(u32.from(f));
    var lo = 0usize;
    var i = 1usize;
    while i < pts.len() {
      if lessPoint(*pts[i], *pts[lo]) { lo = i; }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    var s = String.empty();
    i = 0usize;
    while i < pts.len() {
      let p = *pts[(lo + i) % pts.len()];
      s.appendUInt(u64.from(p.x as u32));
      s.append(",");
      s.appendUInt(u64.from(p.y as u32));
      s.append(",");
      s.appendUInt(u64.from(p.z as u32));
      s.append(";");
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    // insertion, sorted
    var j = out.len();
    out.push(String.from(s.view()));
    while j > 0usize && out[j - 1usize].compare(s.view()) > 0i32 {
      out.set(j, String.from(out[j - 1usize].view()));
      out.set(j - 1usize, String.from(s.view()));
      j = j - 1usize;
    }
    f = f + 1usize;
  }
  out
}

fn lessPoint(p: Vec3, q: Vec3) bool {
  if p.x != q.x { return p.x < q.x; }
  if p.y != q.y { return p.y < q.y; }
  p.z < q.z
}

fn sameFaceSet(a: &PolyMesh, b: &PolyMesh, label: &Array[u8]) {
  let sa = faceSet(a);
  let sb = faceSet(b);
  expectInt(i64.from(sa.len()), i64.from(sb.len()), label);
  var same = sa.len() == sb.len();
  var i = 0usize;
  while same && i < sa.len() {
    if !sa[i].equals(sb[i].view()) { same = false; }
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  expect(same, label);
}

fn exactPredicates() {
  // Kettner et al.: -12u, u = 2^-53
  let u = 0.00000000000000011102230246251565404236316680908203125;
  expectInt(i64.from(orient2dSign(0.5 + u, 0.5, 12.0, 12.0, 24.0, 24.0)), -1, "orient2d Kettner's example");
  expectInt(i64.from(orient2dSign(0.5, 0.5 + u, 12.0, 12.0, 24.0, 24.0)), 1, "orient2d its mirror image");
  let tiny = 0.000000000000000000867361737988403547205962240695953369140625;
  expectInt(i64.from(orient2dSign(0.0, 0.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.5 + 0.0000000000000001, 0.5)), -1, "orient2d right");
  expectInt(i64.from(orient2dSign(0.0, 0.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.5, 0.5 + 0.0000000000000001)), 1, "orient2d left");
  expectInt(i64.from(orient2dSign(0.0, 0.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.5, 0.5)), 0, "orient2d on");
  // Far from the origin, where the f64 products lose the difference
  let big = 1099511627776.0;  // 2^40
  expectInt(i64.from(orient2dSign(big, big, big + 1.0, big + 1.0, big + 2.0, big + 2.0 + tiny * big)), 0,
    "orient2d collinear far out (2^-60 of 2^40 is below an ulp, so the point is on the line)");
  expectInt(i64.from(orient2dSign(big, big, big + 1.0, big + 1.0, big + 2.0, big + 2.000244140625)), 1,
    "orient2d an ulp off the line far out");
  let a = new DVec3(0.0, 0.0, 0.0);
  let b = new DVec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0);
  let c = new DVec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0);
  expectInt(i64.from(orient3dSign(a, b, c, new DVec3(0.25, 0.25, 0.0))), 0, "orient3d in plane");
  expectInt(i64.from(orient3dSign(a, b, c, new DVec3(0.25, 0.25, tiny))), 1, "orient3d just in front");
  expectInt(i64.from(orient3dSign(a, c, b, new DVec3(0.25, 0.25, tiny))), -1, "orient3d turned over");
  // A tilted triangle of f32 points; its centroid's f32 neighbours off it
  let p = new DVec3(f64.from(0.1), f64.from(0.7), f64.from(0.3));
  let q = new DVec3(f64.from(0.9), f64.from(0.2), f64.from(0.4));
  let r = new DVec3(f64.from(0.3), f64.from(0.4), f64.from(0.95));
  expectInt(i64.from(orient3dSign(p, q, r, p)), 0, "orient3d a corner");
  expectInt(i64.from(orient3dSign(p, q, r, new DVec3(0.5, 0.5, 0.5)) * orient3dSign(q, p, r, new DVec3(0.5, 0.5, 0.5))),
    -1, "orient3d swapping two corners flips the sign");
}

fn overlapping() {
  let a = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  let b = moved(PolyMesh.cube(1.), new Vec3(0.5, 0.25, 0.375));
  var p = List[String].empty();
  let u = booleanUnion(&a, &b, &mut p);
  counts(&u, 20, 30, 12, "overlap union counts");
  clean(&u, 11.734375, "overlap union");
  let d = booleanDifference(&a, &b, &mut p);
  counts(&d, 14, 21, 9, "overlap difference counts");
  clean(&d, 3.734375, "overlap difference");
  let n = booleanIntersection(&a, &b, &mut p);
  counts(&n, 8, 12, 6, "overlap intersection counts");
  clean(&n, 4.265625, "overlap intersection");
  expect(hasPoint(&n, 1., 1., 1.), "intersection keeps A's corner");
  expect(hasPoint(&n, -0.5, -0.75, -0.625), "intersection keeps B's corner");
  expect(hasPoint(&n, 1., -0.75, -0.625), "intersection's new corner, exact");
  expectInt(i64.from(p.len()), 0, "overlap reports nothing");
}

fn touching() {
  let a = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  let b = moved(PolyMesh.cube(1.), new Vec3(2., 0., 0.));
  var p = List[String].empty();
  let u = booleanUnion(&a, &b, &mut p);
  counts(&u, 12, 20, 10, "touching union counts");
  clean(&u, 16.0, "touching union");
  let n = booleanIntersection(&a, &b, &mut p);
  counts(&n, 0, 0, 0, "touching intersection is empty");
  let d = booleanDifference(&a, &b, &mut p);
  counts(&d, 8, 12, 6, "touching difference counts");
  clean(&d, 8.0, "touching difference");
  var v = 0u32;
  var corners = true;
  while v < 8u32 {
    let x = if (v & 1u32) != 0u32 {1.f} else {-1.};
    let y = if (v & 2u32) != 0u32 {1.f} else {-1.};
    let z = if (v & 4u32) != 0u32 {1.f} else {-1.};
    if !hasPoint(&d, x, y, z) { corners = false; }
    v = v + 1u32;
  }
  expect(corners, "touching difference is A's corners");
  expectInt(i64.from(p.len()), 0, "touching reports nothing");
}

fn identical() {
  let a = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  var p = List[String].empty();
  let u = booleanUnion(&a, &a, &mut p);
  sameShape(&u, &a, "A u A is A");
  clean(&u, 8.0, "A u A");
  let n = booleanIntersection(&a, &a, &mut p);
  sameShape(&n, &a, "A n A is A");
  let d = booleanDifference(&a, &a, &mut p);
  counts(&d, 0, 0, 0, "A - A is empty");
  let t = torus(1., 0.4, 24u32, 32u32);
  let tu = booleanUnion(&t, &t, &mut p);
  sameShape(&tu, &t, "torus u torus is the torus");
  counts(&tu, 768, 1536, 768, "torus counts");
  let td = booleanDifference(&t, &t, &mut p);
  counts(&td, 0, 0, 0, "torus - torus is empty");
  expectInt(i64.from(p.len()), 0, "identical reports nothing");
}

fn disjoint() {
  let a = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  let b = moved(PolyMesh.cube(1.), new Vec3(3., 0.5, 0.));
  var p = List[String].empty();
  let u = booleanUnion(&a, &b, &mut p);
  counts(&u, 16, 24, 12, "disjoint union counts");
  clean(&u, 16.0, "disjoint union");
  var parts = List[PolyMesh].empty();
  parts.push(PolyMesh.cube(1.));
  parts.push(moved(PolyMesh.cube(1.), new Vec3(3., 0.5, 0.)));
  let j = join(&parts, &mut p);
  sameShape(&u, &j, "disjoint union is the join");
  let d = booleanDifference(&a, &b, &mut p);
  sameShape(&d, &a, "disjoint difference is A");
  let n = booleanIntersection(&a, &b, &mut p);
  counts(&n, 0, 0, 0, "disjoint intersection is empty");
}

fn coplanar() {
  let a = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  let pocket = box(new Vec3(-0.5, -0.5, 0.), new Vec3(0.5, 0.5, 1.));
  var p = List[String].empty();
  let d = booleanDifference(&a, &pocket, &mut p);
  counts(&d, 16, 26, 12, "flush pocket counts");
  clean(&d, 7.0, "flush pocket");
  let u = booleanUnion(&a, &pocket, &mut p);
  counts(&u, 12, 18, 8, "flush union counts");
  clean(&u, 8.0, "flush union");
  let n = booleanIntersection(&a, &pocket, &mut p);
  counts(&n, 8, 12, 6, "flush intersection counts");
  clean(&n, 1.0, "flush intersection");
  let through = box(new Vec3(-0.5, -0.5, -1.), new Vec3(0.5, 0.5, 1.));
  let h = booleanDifference(&a, &through, &mut p);
  counts(&h, 16, 28, 12, "flush hole counts");
  clean(&h, 6.0, "flush hole");
  let half = box(new Vec3(0., -1., -1.), new Vec3(2., 1., 1.));
  let hu = booleanUnion(&a, &half, &mut p);
  counts(&hu, 12, 20, 10, "half overlap union counts");
  clean(&hu, 12.0, "half overlap union");
  let hd = booleanDifference(&a, &half, &mut p);
  counts(&hd, 8, 12, 6, "half overlap difference counts");
  clean(&hd, 4.0, "half overlap difference");
  let hn = booleanIntersection(&a, &half, &mut p);
  counts(&hn, 8, 12, 6, "half overlap intersection counts");
  clean(&hn, 4.0, "half overlap intersection");
  expectInt(i64.from(p.len()), 0, "coplanar reports nothing");
}

fn prismThrough() {
  let a = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  let b = prism(16u32, 0.5, 0.1, 0.05, -2., 2.);
  // The section's area from its own f32 corners
  let prof = Profile.circle(16u32, 0.5);
  var s = 0.0;
  var i = 0usize;
  while i < 16usize {
    let p = *prof.points[i];
    let q = *prof.points[(i + 1usize) % 16usize];
    s = s + f64.from(p.x) * f64.from(q.y) - f64.from(q.x) * f64.from(p.y);
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  s = s * 0.5;
  expectFloat(s, 0.76536686, 0.000001, "prism section by hand");
  var pr = List[String].empty();
  let d = booleanDifference(&a, &b, &mut pr);
  counts(&d, 44, 68, 24, "prism difference counts");
  clean(&d, 8.0 - 2.0 * s, "prism difference");
  let u = booleanUnion(&a, &b, &mut pr);
  counts(&u, 76, 116, 42, "prism union counts");
  clean(&u, 8.0 + 2.0 * s, "prism union");
  let n = booleanIntersection(&a, &b, &mut pr);
  counts(&n, 32, 48, 18, "prism intersection counts");
  clean(&n, 2.0 * s, "prism intersection");
  expectInt(i64.from(pr.len()), 0, "prism reports nothing");
}

fn pocketInTriangle() {
  var a = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  let id = a.addFloatChannel(FaceDomain, "id", 0.);
  var f = 0u32;
  while f < 6u32 {
    a.setFloat(id, f, f32.from(f));
    f = f + 1u32;
  }
  let b = box(new Vec3(0.3, -0.6, 0.5), new Vec3(0.6, -0.3, 1.5));
  var p = List[String].empty();
  let d = booleanDifference(&a, &b, &mut p);
  counts(&d, 16, 26, 12, "pocket in a triangle counts");
  clean(&d, 7.955, "pocket in a triangle");
  let ch = d.findFloatChannel(FaceDomain, "id");
  var front = 0.0;
  var pieces = 0i64;
  f = 0u32;
  while usize.from(f) < d.faceCount() {
    if d.float(ch, f) == 1. {
      front = front + faceArea(&d, f);
      pieces = pieces + 1;
    }
    f = f + 1u32;
  }
  expectFloat(front, 3.91, 0.00001, "the front face round the pocket");
  expectInt(pieces, 2, "the front face as two pieces");
  let u = booleanUnion(&a, &b, &mut p);
  clean(&u, 8.045, "pocket union");
  let n = booleanIntersection(&a, &b, &mut p);
  clean(&n, 0.045, "pocket intersection");
  expectInt(i64.from(p.len()), 0, "pocket reports nothing");
}

fn edgeTouching() {
  let a = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  let b = box(new Vec3(1., 1., -1.), new Vec3(3., 3., 1.));
  var p = List[String].empty();
  let u = booleanUnion(&a, &b, &mut p);
  solid(&u, 16.0, "edge touching union");
  expectInt(i64.from(p.len()), 1, "edge touching union says so");
  var q = List[String].empty();
  let d = booleanDifference(&a, &b, &mut q);
  counts(&d, 8, 12, 6, "edge touching difference counts");
  clean(&d, 8.0, "edge touching difference");
  let n = booleanIntersection(&a, &b, &mut q);
  counts(&n, 0, 0, 0, "edge touching intersection is empty");
  expectInt(i64.from(q.len()), 0, "edge touching difference reports nothing");
}

fn tori() {
  let a = torus(1., 0.4, 24u32, 32u32);
  let b = placed(torus(1., 0.4, 24u32, 32u32), new Transform3(new Vec3(0.7, 0.13, 0.21),
    Quat.angleAxis(1.1, new Vec3(1., 0.2, 0.1).normalize()), new Vec3(1., 1., 1.)));
  var p = List[String].empty();
  let u = booleanUnion(&a, &b, &mut p);
  let d = booleanDifference(&a, &b, &mut p);
  let n = booleanIntersection(&a, &b, &mut p);
  let va = volume(&a);
  let vu = volume(&u);
  let vd = volume(&d);
  let vn = volume(&n);
  clean(&u, vu, "tori union");
  clean(&d, vd, "tori difference");
  clean(&n, vn, "tori intersection");
  expectFloat((vu + vn) / (2.0 * va), 1.0, 0.00001, "union and intersection add to both");
  expectFloat((vd + vn) / va, 1.0, 0.00001, "difference and intersection add to A");
  expect(vn > 0.1 && vn < va - 0.1, "the tori overlap in part");
  expectInt(i64.from(p.len()), 0, "tori report nothing");
}

// B with its faces listed backward and its vertices numbered backward
fn shuffled(m: &PolyMesh) PolyMesh {
  let nv = m.vertexCount();
  var pos = List[Vec3].withCapacity(nv);
  var v = 0usize;
  while v < nv {
    pos.push(*m.positions[nv - 1usize - v]);
    v = v + 1usize;
  }
  var cnt = List[u32].empty();
  var idx = List[u32].empty();
  var f = m.faceCount();
  while f > 0usize {
    f = f - 1usize;
    let vs = m.faceVertices(u32.from(f));
    cnt.push(u32.from(vs.len()));
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < vs.len() {
      idx.push(u32.from(nv - 1usize) - *vs[i]);
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
  }
  var problems = List[String].empty();
  PolyMesh.fromPolygons(pos.view(), cnt.view(), idx.view(), &mut problems)
}

fn order() {
  let a = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  let b = moved(PolyMesh.cube(1.), new Vec3(0.5, 0.25, 0.375));
  let b2 = shuffled(&b);
  var p = List[String].empty();
  let u1 = booleanUnion(&a, &b, &mut p);
  let u2 = booleanUnion(&a, &b2, &mut p);
  sameFaceSet(&u1, &u2, "union whatever B's order");
  let d1 = booleanDifference(&a, &b, &mut p);
  let d2 = booleanDifference(&a, &b2, &mut p);
  sameFaceSet(&d1, &d2, "difference whatever B's order");
  let t = torus(1., 0.4, 12u32, 16u32);
  let s = placed(torus(1., 0.4, 12u32, 16u32), new Transform3(new Vec3(0.3, 0.1, 0.2),
    Quat.angleAxis(0.7, new Vec3(0., 0., 1.)), new Vec3(1., 1., 1.)));
  let n1 = booleanIntersection(&t, &s, &mut p);
  let n2 = booleanIntersection(&shuffled(&t), &shuffled(&s), &mut p);
  sameFaceSet(&n1, &n2, "tori intersection whatever their order");
  // The same bits twice
  let again = booleanUnion(&a, &b, &mut p);
  sameShape(&u1, &again, "the same bits twice");
}

fn channels() {
  var a = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  var b = moved(PolyMesh.cube(1.), new Vec3(0.5, 0.25, 0.375));
  dress(&mut a, 0.);
  dress(&mut b, 10.);
  let wch = a.addFloatChannel(VertexDomain, "weight", 1.);
  var v = 0u32;
  while v < 8u32 { a.setFloat(wch, v, 0.5); v = v + 1u32; }
  // A's edge from vertex 3 (1, 1, -1) to 7 (1, 1, 1)
  let cr = a.addFloatChannel(EdgeDomain, "crease", 0.);
  var e = 0u32;
  while usize.from(e) < a.edgeCount() {
    let x = a.fromVertex(2u32 * e);
    let y = a.toVertex(2u32 * e);
    if (x == 3u32 && y == 7u32) || (x == 7u32 && y == 3u32) { a.setFloat(cr, e, 2.); }
    e = e + 1u32;
  }
  var p = List[String].empty();
  let n = booleanIntersection(&a, &b, &mut p);
  expectInt(i64.from(p.len()), 0, "channels report nothing");
  let w = n.findFloatChannel(VertexDomain, "w");
  let uv = n.findVec2Channel(CornerDomain, "uv");
  let id = n.findFloatChannel(FaceDomain, "id");
  let wt = n.findFloatChannel(VertexDomain, "weight");
  let cn = n.findFloatChannel(EdgeDomain, "crease");
  expect(w != NoIndex && uv != NoIndex && id != NoIndex && wt != NoIndex && cn != NoIndex, "channels carried");
  var wOk = true;
  v = 0u32;
  while usize.from(v) < n.vertexCount() {
    let q = *n.positions[usize.from(v)];
    if absd(f64.from(n.float(w, v)) - f64.from(q.x + 2. * q.y + 3. * q.z)) > 0.00001 { wOk = false; }
    v = v + 1u32;
  }
  expect(wOk, "w is x + 2y + 3z at every vertex");
  var uvOk = true;
  var f = 0u32;
  var ids = 0u32;
  while usize.from(f) < n.faceCount() {
    let hs = n.faceHalfedges(f);
    var k = 0usize;
    while k < hs.len() {
      let q = *n.positions[usize.from(n.toVertex(*hs[k]))];
      let t = n.vec2(uv, *hs[k]);
      if absd(f64.from(t.x - q.x)) > 0.00001 || absd(f64.from(t.y - q.y)) > 0.00001 { uvOk = false; }
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    ids = ids | (1u32 << u32.from(n.float(id, f)));
    f = f + 1u32;
  }
  expect(uvOk, "uv is (x, y) at every corner");
  // A's front 1, right 3, top 5; B's back 10, left 12, bottom 14
  expectUInt(u64.from(ids), u64.from((1u32 << 1u32) | (1u32 << 3u32) | (1u32 << 5u32) | (1u32 << 10u32) | (1u32 << 12u32)
    | (1u32 << 14u32)), "faces' ids");
  var crease2 = 0i64;
  var creaseOther = 0i64;
  e = 0u32;
  while usize.from(e) < n.edgeCount() {
    let c = n.float(cn, e);
    let x = *n.positions[usize.from(n.fromVertex(2u32 * e))];
    let y = *n.positions[usize.from(n.toVertex(2u32 * e))];
    if c == 2. && x.x == 1. && x.y == 1. && y.x == 1. && y.y == 1. { crease2 = crease2 + 1; }
    elif c != 0. { creaseOther = creaseOther + 1; }
    e = e + 1u32;
  }
  expectInt(crease2, 1, "the crease edge's piece keeps 2");
  expectInt(creaseOther, 0, "every other edge is 0");
  v = 0u32;
  var wB = 0.;
  var wA = 0.;
  while usize.from(v) < n.vertexCount() {
    let q = *n.positions[usize.from(v)];
    if q.x == -0.5 && q.y == -0.75 && q.z == -0.625 { wB = n.float(wt, v); }
    if q.x == 1. && q.y == 1. && q.z == 1. { wA = n.float(wt, v); }
    v = v + 1u32;
  }
  expectFloat(f64.from(wB), 1.0, near, "B's corner takes the weight's fill");
  expectFloat(f64.from(wA), 0.5, near, "A's corner keeps its weight");

  // The curve creased
  let c3 = booleanWith(&a, &b, BooleanIntersection, 3., &mut p);
  let cc = c3.findFloatChannel(EdgeDomain, "crease");
  var three = 0i64;
  var two = 0i64;
  e = 0u32;
  while usize.from(e) < c3.edgeCount() {
    if c3.float(cc, e) == 3. { three = three + 1; }
    if c3.float(cc, e) == 2. { two = two + 1; }
    e = e + 1u32;
  }
  expectInt(three, 6, "six curve edges creased 3");
  expectInt(two, 1, "the crease edge still 2");
  let plainA = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  let plainB = moved(PolyMesh.cube(1.), new Vec3(0.5, 0.25, 0.375));
  let made = booleanWith(&plainA, &plainB, BooleanIntersection, 3., &mut p);
  let mc = made.findFloatChannel(EdgeDomain, "crease");
  expect(mc != NoIndex, "a crease channel made");
  three = 0i64;
  var zero = 0i64;
  e = 0u32;
  while mc != NoIndex && usize.from(e) < made.edgeCount() {
    if made.float(mc, e) == 3. { three = three + 1; }
    if made.float(mc, e) == 0. { zero = zero + 1; }
    e = e + 1u32;
  }
  expectInt(three, 6, "made: six curve edges 3");
  expectInt(zero, 6, "made: the rest 0");

  // A clash refused, the result still made
  var c = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  let cw = c.addFloatChannel(VertexDomain, "w", 0.);
  c.setFloat(cw, 0u32, 1.);
  var dd = moved(PolyMesh.cube(1.), new Vec3(0.5, 0.25, 0.375));
  dd.addVec2Channel(FaceDomain, "w", new Vec2(0., 0.));
  var q = List[String].empty();
  let r = booleanUnion(&c, &dd, &mut q);
  expectInt(i64.from(q.len()), 1, "a clash is one line");
  if q.len() > 0usize { expectStr(q[0usize].view(), "part 1's channel w (Vec2, face) is left out: part 0 has it as f32", "the clash's line"); }
  clean(&r, 11.734375, "the result still made");
}

// Channels: vertex "w" = x + 2y + 3z, face "id" from 'base', corner "uv" (x, y)
fn dress(m: &mut PolyMesh, base: f32) {
  let w = m.addFloatChannel(VertexDomain, "w", 0.);
  var v = 0u32;
  while usize.from(v) < m.vertexCount() {
    let p = *m.positions[usize.from(v)];
    m.setFloat(w, v, p.x + 2. * p.y + 3. * p.z);
    v = v + 1u32;
  }
  let id = m.addFloatChannel(FaceDomain, "id", 0.);
  var f = 0u32;
  while usize.from(f) < m.faceCount() {
    m.setFloat(id, f, base + f32.from(f));
    f = f + 1u32;
  }
  let uv = m.addVec2Channel(CornerDomain, "uv", new Vec2(0., 0.));
  var h = 0u32;
  while usize.from(h) < m.halfedgeCount() {
    let p = *m.positions[usize.from(m.toVertex(h))];
    m.setVec2(uv, h, new Vec2(p.x, p.y));
    h = h + 1u32;
  }
}

fn absd(a: f64) f64 {if a < 0.0 {-a} else {a}}

fn refused() {
  let pts: Array[Vec3, 4] = [new Vec3(0., 0., 0.), new Vec3(1., 0., 0.), new Vec3(1., 1., 0.), new Vec3(0., 1., 0.)];
  let cnt: Array[u32, 1] = [4u32];
  let idx: Array[u32, 4] = [0u32, 1u32, 2u32, 3u32];
  var p = List[String].empty();
  let quad = PolyMesh.fromPolygons(&pts, &cnt, &idx, &mut p);
  let r = booleanUnion(&quad, &PolyMesh.cube(1.), &mut p);
  counts(&r, 0, 0, 0, "an open mesh gives nothing");
  expectInt(i64.from(p.len()), 1, "an open mesh is one line");
  if p.len() > 0usize { expectStr(p[0usize].view(), "the first mesh is not closed: 4 edges have a face on one side only", "open line"); }
  // A cube with every face turned over
  let cube = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  var cps = List[Vec3].empty();
  var v = 0usize;
  while v < 8usize { cps.push(*cube.positions[v]); v = v + 1usize; }
  var ccnt = List[u32].empty();
  var cidx = List[u32].empty();
  var f = 0u32;
  while f < 6u32 {
    let vs = cube.faceVertices(f);
    ccnt.push(4u32);
    var i = 4usize;
    while i > 0usize {
      i = i - 1usize;
      cidx.push(*vs[i]);
    }
    f = f + 1u32;
  }
  var q = List[String].empty();
  let inside = PolyMesh.fromPolygons(cps.view(), ccnt.view(), cidx.view(), &mut q);
  let r2 = booleanDifference(&PolyMesh.cube(1.), &inside, &mut q);
  counts(&r2, 0, 0, 0, "an inside-out mesh gives nothing");
  expectInt(i64.from(q.len()), 1, "an inside-out mesh is one line");
  if q.len() > 0usize { expectStr(q[0usize].view(), "the second mesh faces inward (its volume is not positive)", "inward line"); }
}

// Faces that are flat, pass a point twice, or have two sides overlapping on
// a line (a spike or a slit), at the rounded points: 0 for a clean result
fn degenerateFaces(m: &PolyMesh) i64 {
  var n = 0i64;
  var f = 0usize;
  while f < m.faceCount() {
    let pts = m.facePositions(u32.from(f));
    let k = pts.len();
    var bad = false;
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < k {
      let a = DVec3.from(*pts[i]);
      let b = DVec3.from(*pts[(i + 1usize) % k]);
      var j = 0usize;
      while j < k {
        if j != i {
          let c = DVec3.from(*pts[j]);
          let d = DVec3.from(*pts[(j + 1usize) % k]);
          if c.x == a.x && c.y == a.y && c.z == a.z { bad = true; }
          let u = b - a;
          let v1 = c - a;
          let v2 = d - a;
          let c1 = new DVec3(u.y * v1.z - u.z * v1.y, u.z * v1.x - u.x * v1.z, u.x * v1.y - u.y * v1.x);
          let c2 = new DVec3(u.y * v2.z - u.z * v2.y, u.z * v2.x - u.x * v2.z, u.x * v2.y - u.y * v2.x);
          if c1.dot(c1) == 0.0 && c2.dot(c2) == 0.0 && u.dot(u) > 0.0 {
            let l = u.dot(u);
            let t1 = v1.dot(u) / l;
            let t2 = v2.dot(u) / l;
            let lo = if t1 < t2 {t1} else {t2};
            let hi = if t1 < t2 {t2} else {t1};
            let olo = if lo > 0.0 {lo} else {0.0};
            let ohi = if hi < 1.0 {hi} else {1.0};
            if ohi > olo { bad = true; }
          }
        }
        j = j + 1usize;
      }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    if bad { n = n + 1; }
    f = f + 1usize;
  }
  n
}

// Boxes stacked face to face and sharing a side plane, where the
// perturbation's slivers fold into the faces: the union is clean
fn stacked() {
  let top = box(new Vec3(-0.25, -0.75, 0.5), new Vec3(0.5, 0.75, 0.75));
  let low = box(new Vec3(0.25, -0.75, 0.), new Vec3(0.75, 0.25, 0.5));
  var p = List[String].empty();
  let u = booleanUnion(&top, &low, &mut p);
  counts(&u, 17, 27, 12, "stacked union counts");
  clean(&u, 0.53125, "stacked union");
  expectInt(degenerateFaces(&u), 0, "stacked union has no face of no area");
  expectInt(i64.from(p.len()), 0, "stacked reports nothing");
  // A plus sign of two bars sharing their top and bottom planes, slotted
  // through its top by a box: 0.5 + 0.5 - 0.125, less 0.2 x 2 x 0.25
  let bar1 = box(new Vec3(-1., -0.25, 0.), new Vec3(1., 0.25, 0.5));
  let bar2 = box(new Vec3(-0.25, -1., 0.), new Vec3(0.25, 1., 0.5));
  let plus = booleanUnion(&bar1, &bar2, &mut p);
  clean(&plus, 0.875, "plus");
  expectInt(degenerateFaces(&plus), 0, "plus has no face of no area");
  let slot = box(new Vec3(-0.1, -2., 0.25), new Vec3(0.1, 2., 1.));
  let slotted = booleanDifference(&plus, &slot, &mut p);
  clean(&slotted, 0.775, "slotted plus");
  expectInt(degenerateFaces(&slotted), 0, "slotted plus has no face of no area");
  // and used again: its intersection with a box holding it is itself
  let held = booleanIntersection(&slotted, &box(new Vec3(-3., -3., -3.), new Vec3(3., 3., 3.)), &mut p);
  clean(&held, 0.775, "the slotted plus used again");
  expectInt(i64.from(p.len()), 0, "plus reports nothing");
  // Two boxes touching along an edge, kept manifold by edges of no length
  // (reported), are refused as an input: such an edge's triangle has no area
  let a = PolyMesh.cube(1.);
  let b = box(new Vec3(1., 1., -1.), new Vec3(3., 3., 1.));
  var q = List[String].empty();
  let pair = booleanUnion(&a, &b, &mut q);
  var q2 = List[String].empty();
  let three = booleanUnion(&pair, &box(new Vec3(5., 0., 0.), new Vec3(7., 2., 2.)), &mut q2);
  counts(&three, 0, 0, 0, "a result with edges of no length is refused as input");
  expectInt(i64.from(q2.len()), 1, "with one line");
  if q2.len() > 0usize { expect(q2[0usize].contains("an edge of no length"), "saying so"); }
}

fn main() i32 {
  exactPredicates();
  stacked();
  overlapping();
  touching();
  identical();
  disjoint();
  coplanar();
  prismThrough();
  pocketInTriangle();
  edgeTouching();
  tori();
  order();
  channels();
  refused();
  done()
}
